<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Xin (Qin)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Xin was a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> during its wars of unification. He pursued the crown prince of Yan, Dan, after the attempt on the life of the future First Emperor, and in 225 BCE led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> army of about 200,000 men against Chu, which was routed by the Chu general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yan">Xiang Yan</a>. He later served in the conquests of Yan and Qi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-xin-qin.jpg" alt="Li Xin (Qin)" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 選者:余邵魚（明）／校訂者:陳継儒（明） · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NAJDA-308-0236_%E6%96%B0%E9%90%AB%E9%99%B3%E7%9C%89%E5%85%AC%E5%85%88%E7%94%9F%E6%89%B9%E8%A9%95%E6%98%A5%E7%A7%8B%E5%88%97%E5%9B%BD%E5%BF%97%E4%BC%9D_%E5%B7%BB1_(%E6%9D%8E%E4%BF%A1%E4%BB%A5%E7%9C%BE%E5%BE%81%E6%A5%9A%E5%9C%8B).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
